{#
  Which kind of collection a record is, and therefore which template renders it.

  collectionIsMajor was a checkbox answering "does this deserve a landing page",
  which is a question about effort rather than about the material. A column run
  of 219 pieces deserves a landing page and must not get a Start reading button.
  collectionKind answers the question that matters.

  A macro rather than an include, because an include has its own scope and a
  variable set inside one does not reach the caller. The collections index needs
  the same answer, so it has to be callable.

      {% import "collections/_kind" as ck %}
      {% set kind = ck.of(entry) %}

  Read through the layout: a custom field reads as defined on a type that has no
  such field and throws the moment it is read. Where the field does not exist
  yet, or is empty, the old checkbox still decides, so this is correct before
  the field is applied and after.
#}
{% macro of(entry) %}
  {%- set handles = [] -%}
  {%- for f in entry.fieldLayout.customFields -%}{%- set handles = handles|merge([f.handle]) -%}{%- endfor -%}
  {%- set k = 'collectionKind' in handles ? (attribute(entry, 'collectionKind') ?? '')|trim : '' -%}
  {%- if k == '' -%}
    {%- set k = ('collectionIsMajor' in handles and entry.collectionIsMajor) ? 'book' : '' -%}
  {%- endif -%}
  {{- k -}}
{% endmacro %}
